Nethack save files are stored in binary which is OS specific so, in
general, you can't transfer save files between different OSes (e.g. from
UNIX to MS Win32).

However, between two Win32 systems at least, you can get round the
different login names problem by renaming the file. So if your Nethack
character's name is Conan started on computer1 where your system
login name is Alice then you'll have a save file called:

alice-Conan.NetHack-saved-game

On computer2 let's say your login name is Bob. To use the save file
on this machine, rename it to:

bob-Conan.Nethack-saved-game

This works for me between two MS WinXP machines but I can't
guarantee it would work under other OSes - and as noted, it won't
work between machines with different OSes.

